    92	**Line 3, later details: the shipped renderer, as the Step 2 log §12 measured it.**
    93	- **Population:** groups whose original has at least one later report.
    94	- **Sample:** 30 at random.
    95	- **The two renderings:**
    96	  - "grouped": the frozen dossier, `step3/library.group_text(member_text=True)`;
    97	  - "apart": each member as its own entry, `record_text`.
    98	  - Any loss the frozen renderer causes, such as a later report's tier, stated day, period or speaker, counts against it.
    99	- **An independent detail key, of content only** (the council's round-8 consensus, D675):
   100	  - **A detail** is what a later report's statement adds to its group's original: "a figure, condition, party, date or qualification an
   101	    analyst would want to keep" (the Step 2 reference's question 2; PRD §6, "details a later report adds, such as a guidance
   102	    condition"; the recorded test's "detail" category).
   103	  - The record's own attribution fields (tier, stated day, period, reporting speaker) are not shown to the key readers, so the key
   104	    holds content by construction. A party or period that changes the claim still counts when the statement's own text says it.
   105	  - Two closed key readers, one per family, each list the details. A third session settles every detail they do not share.
   106	  - The key is frozen before either rendering is read.
   107	- **Reading:**
   108	  - Each rendering of a group goes to its own closed session in each family: four sessions per group. No session sees both renderings,
   109	    as in the recorded test, where each reader read one view.
   110	  - Both renderings carry the same surrounding dossier: the other groups under the same thesis, each as its original's record.
   111	  - The session marks which key details its rendering states.
   112	- **Pass:** over the 30 groups, the grouped rendering's detail total is no fewer than the apart rendering's, summed over both families,
   113	  as the recorded test summed both readers. Each family's totals are printed beside.
   114	  - The mean paired difference per group is printed with a 95% bootstrap interval over groups.
   115	  - Fewer than 30 groups: **not measured**.
   116	- **Printed beside:** the count of later reports whose tier, stated day, period or speaker differs from the original's (the fields
   117	  `group_text` drops), counted by code.
   118	- **Disclosed with the result:** both renderings carry the same content, so the line checks that grouping loses no content a later
   119	  report adds, against the readers' own noise. It is weaker than the recorded test's unprompted questions.
   120	
   121	Lines 1 and 2 are decided on their point estimates, with a Wilson 95% interval printed beside.
